#: ../doc/preferences.rst:210
msgid "The :guilabel:`Auto-Optimize` choices work as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:212
msgid ":guilabel:`Ask`: show a banner when qualifying videos are found. Accepting enables automatic optimization for that project; dismissing remembers your decision."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:214
msgid ":guilabel:`Always`: automatically optimize qualifying videos without a banner."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:215
msgid ":guilabel:`Never`: do not show the banner or start automatic optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:217
msgid "These are defaults, not overrides of saved project choices. For example, selecting :guilabel:`Never` here does not turn off a project where you already enabled :menuselection:`File --> Auto-Optimize`. Use that menu item to change the current project's setting. Manual optimization remains available with every preference."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:222
msgid "The threshold is measured in milliseconds (**ms**). With the default **200 ms**, a video with a recorded time of 350 ms qualifies, while one with a time of 50 ms does not. Changing the threshold re-evaluates existing timings without decoding videos again; it does not cancel jobs already queued or running."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:227
msgid "The timing comes from normal thumbnail generation. Older projects without saved timings are checked in the background, one small thumbnail at a time, when Auto-Optimize is set to Ask or Always (or enabled from the File menu). It excludes opening the file, writing the thumbnail image, and waiting in a queue. It is saved with the project's file information and reused on the same computer while the source file is unchanged. See :ref:`optimize_ref` for the banner, status indicators, and manual optimization options."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:236
msgid "Autosave"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/preferences.rst:240
msgid "Autosave is a feature in OpenShot which automatically saves the current changes to your project after a specific number of minutes, helping to reduce the risk or impact of data loss in case of a crash, freeze or user error."
msgstr ""

